from gratipay.utils import markdown
[---]
banner = _("API")
title = _("Gratipay Docs")
[---] text/html
{% extends "templates/api.html" %}
{% block content %}{{ markdown.render("""

You've found the Gratipay API, version 2!

These pages also serve as the top-level documentation for all of Gratipay as a
software application. Technically speaking, we have a few layers:

 - **Database**&mdash;We store our data in [PostgreSQL
   9.3](http://www.postgresql.org/docs/9.3/static/), and we write a fair amount
of the [Postgres dialect of
SQL](http://www.postgresql.org/docs/9.3/static/sql.html). We use and maintain
the [postgres.py](http://postgres-py.readthedocs.org/) client library.

 - **Website**&mdash;The Gratipay.com website includes UI, API, and admin all
   in one. This hopefully makes it easier for you to [get up and running
locally](https://github.com/gratipay/gratipay.com#quick-start): install one
app, and you have everything you need to hack on Gratipay all in one place. We
use and maintain our own server-side web framework, [Aspen](http://aspen.io/).
We use [Python 2](https://docs.python.org/release/2.7.9/), the SCSS syntax for
[Sass](http://sass-lang.com/), [jQuery 1](https://jquery.com/), and the admin
dashboard uses [Backbone](http://backbonejs.org/).

 - **Payday**&mdash;We process payments on a weekly cycle, using a combination
   of Python and Bash scripts.

Conceptually speaking, Gratipay is an
[accounting](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accounting) application, with a
general ledger and chart of [accounts](/api/v2/accounts/) at its heart.


## How To Use This API

Many of the HTTP resources under [`/api/v2/`](/api/v2/) that you're browsing
right now as `text/html` also have JSON representations. Set the `Accept`
header to `application/json` to request the JSON version:

```
$ curl -H \"Accept: application/json\" https://gratipay.com/api/v2/foo/
```

## Authentication

Use the user id and API key from [your settings page](/about/me/settings) to
authenticate your requests:

```
$ curl -H \"Accept: application/json\" -u $user_id:$api_key https://gratipay.com/api/v2/foo/
```

""" )}}{% endblock %}
